This directory contains various SIPP-related things that people have
sent us.  Some are functions for creating new objects some are
intresting things which uses SIPP some are enhancements on top of
SIPP. Some of these things might be included in future releases of
SIPP but we make no promises.

In all cases we simply have NO possibility to support the things in
here or to keep them up to date and we can NOT guarantee that any of
them is working. If you run inte trouble with something, turn to the
original author! We will try to keep a list of them up to date in
this file.


Currently this directory contains:
xrender.c:
        Use SIPP to render in an X window. Can do fast preview with
        subsampling and some other fun features.
        Author: Rene Mueller <kiwi@iis.ethz.ch>

xchain.c:
        chain.c from the demo directory with minor modifications to
        use the above xrender function.
        Author: Jonas Yngvesson <jonas-y@isy.liu.se>

snail.c:
        Function to create a "snail" or "shell" object in SIPP.
        Author: Rene Mueller <kiwi@iis.ethz.ch>

superquad.c:
        Function to create a superquadric object in SIPP.
        Author: Rene Mueller <kiwi@iis.ethz.ch>
